    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c1-b17b-f687acf51c15",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "❓ "
        ],
        [
          "What is Spring Security and how does in-memory authentication work?",
          [
            [
              "i"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8025-b97b-cba024755564",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "\"Spring Security is a framework that helps protect applications by adding authentication and authorization. In-memory authentication is a simple way to define users and roles directly in the code, without using a database. It’s mainly used for testing or learning. I typically configure it with a "
        ],
        [
          "UserDetailsService",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", define roles, and use "
        ],
        [
          "BCryptPasswordEncoder",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " to securely store passwords.\""
        ]
      ]
    },
