    {
      "id": "ed-security-version",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot 3 and Spring Security 6"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-security-version-b0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot 3 uses Spring Security 6 and requires Java 17 or later. Configure a SecurityFilterChain bean with authorizeHttpRequests and requestMatchers."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-security-version-b1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The Engineering Digest journal repository uses Spring Boot 2.7. Its WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter, antMatchers and javax.servlet imports belong to that older version. New servlet imports use jakarta.servlet."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-security-version-b2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Authentication establishes the current user. Authorization checks permissions. Ownership checks whether that user may access a particular journal entry. These are separate checks."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-security-version-b3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A role protects a group of operations. It does not prove that a user owns the requested record."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-security-version-b4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Keep CSRF protection for browser sessions. A stateless session policy alone does not make an application safe from CSRF. Decide from how the browser sends credentials."
        ]
      ]
    },
